+
+## Page end effects (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01. Owner requests an end effect like the track list at both menu ends. Static-content outward pulls now resist at Race's first edge (including its concurrent rivalry view) and Garage's last edge. Only the clipped body/scenery moves; navigation stays fixed. The pull matches the carousel: 64 logical-unit cap, `1-exp(-distance/160)` resistance, and a 380 ms `TRANS_BACK` ease-out return. There is no wrapping. Release, cancellation and a second finger settle the pull; a new gesture, navigation or race start clears an active return. Track-carousel overscroll remains independent.
+
+Changed files: `game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` emits gesture lifecycle/drag signals; `game/core/app.gd` owns the separate edge-return tween; `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd` checks both directions, resistance/cap, fixed header, spring motion/settlement, cancellation, two fingers, navigation interruption and separate carousel overscroll. This document, status/plan notes and `docs/evidence/menu-end-effects-2026-10-04/` retain verification. No canonical/rules/schema changes; concurrent rivalry work is preserved.
+
